### Expected Results

`AndroidSurfaceGLImpeller` and `EmbedderSurfaceGLImpeller` should lazily initialize a single `std::shared_ptr<impeller::AiksContext>` once the GL context is current on the raster thread and share it across `GPUSurfaceGLImpeller` instances (matching how the Metal backend shares `AiksContext` across `GPUSurfaceMetalImpeller` instances since [#145053](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/pull/145053)), so `ContentContext` and its default pipelines are only created once.

### Actual Results

On the raster thread in the startup trace:
- `ContentContext` runs **$N + 1$ times** when $N$ `Picture.toImageSync()` calls execute before the onscreen surface is created (3 times in the repro above, or 3 times for a single `Picture.toImageSync()` call prior to [#194506](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/pull/194506)).
- Recreating the `SurfaceView` (e.g., backgrounding and foregrounding the app) also reconstructs `AiksContext` and recompiles all default pipelines.

