#192724 explains the cause and fixes it. In the branch for a node whose geometry became invisible, `parentInSemanticsTree.firstAncestorNodeWithCleanGeometry` is read without calling `computeAncestorInfo(treeShapeToken)` first. The value can be left over from an earlier flush and point at a node whose geometry has since been cleared, so `ensureSemanticsNode()` runs on a node with `geometry == null`.

The error is caught by `FlutterError.reportError` after the frame has been composited, so the app does not die. But that flush stops partway: `_nodesNeedingSemanticsUpdate` was already cleared, the remaining nodes are never processed, and `sendSemanticsUpdate()` is skipped, so the platform keeps a stale tree until those nodes change again.

This issue is filed so #192724 has an issue to link to (as requested in that PR). Related: #184036 (fixed by #184226, a different path) and #189908 (an `owner!` read in the same flush).

