Related to #194773, which reports that on 3.47.7 the text shadow cache misses almost every frame, as allocation churn on OpenGLES. On Vulkan the same misses do not give the memory back: the native heap grows without bound.

### Steps to reproduce

1. Run the code sample below in release mode on an Android device that uses Impeller with Vulkan (tested on a POCO F5: Snapdragon 7+ Gen 2 / Adreno 725, Android 16, display at 60 Hz).
2. Sample the app's native heap every 10 s with `adb shell dumpsys meminfo <package>`.

The sample rebuilds two `Text`s with a blurred `Shadow` every frame: a counter that changes every frame and a label that never changes. `--dart-define=MODE=changing|static|both` and `--dart-define=BLUR=<blurRadius>` pick the variant.

### Expected results

The native heap stays flat, as it does with `blurRadius: 0`.

### Actual results

The native heap grows linearly and is never given back (release, KB/s of `Native Heap` over 60 s):

| MODE | blurRadius | Native Heap growth |
|---|---|---|
| both (changing counter + unchanged label) | 4 | **123 KB/s** |
| changing counter only | 4 | **66 KB/s** |
| unchanged label only (rebuilt, never repainted) | 4 | 8 KB/s |
| both | 0 | 14 KB/s |

`Graphics` in `dumpsys meminfo` stays around 1 MB; only `Native Heap` grows. A full Dart GC (VM service `getAllocationProfile` with `gc: true`) does not bring it down, and the Dart heap stays small, so the memory is held on the engine side.

The unchanged label adds to the growth once it is repainted together with the changing counter (123 vs 66 KB/s), which matches what #194773 sees on this version: even unchanged text misses the text shadow cache every frame. #194773 reports the misses as allocation churn on OpenGLES; on Vulkan here the memory does not come back.

In our game (Flame, a HUD with about ten shadowed labels redrawn every frame by a moving clock) the same thing grew the native heap by about 270 KB/s: from 34 MB at start to 775 MB after 27 minutes, PSS 891 MB. Freezing the HUD (same widgets, no repaint) or removing the blur from its text shadows brings the growth down to the level of the rest of the app (5–15 KB/s).

Not tested on beta or master yet; #190681 in 3.50 may cover the unchanged-label case.

