### Steps to reproduce

1. Build a bare `EditableText` (not a `TextField`) whose controller holds some text.
2. Focus it, unfocus it, then focus it again. On the second focus the selection is already valid: collapsed at the end, from the first focus.
3. Read `RenderEditable.hasFocus` and the `isFocused` flag on the text field's semantics node.

The test below does this, and runs the same steps on a `TextField` for comparison.

### Expected results

After the second focus, `RenderEditable.hasFocus` is true and the text field's semantics node has `isFocused`, as after the first focus and as with `TextField`.

### Actual results

`FocusNode.hasFocus` is true, but `RenderEditable.hasFocus` and the semantics `isFocused` flag stay false, still false two seconds later. The `TextField` test passes.

On web with semantics enabled, this drops input: we hit it in a chat composer built on `EditableText`, where text typed after the field was refocused never reached it, although the caret was drawn. The engine activates semantics text editing only for a text field whose node reports focus ([`SemanticTextField.update`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/5fc346839b5d0eef006ed8404392afb4dfae428d/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/semantics/text_field.dart#L314-L330)).

As far as I can tell:
- [`_handleFocusChanged`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/5fc346839b5d0eef006ed8404392afb4dfae428d/packages/flutter/lib/src/widgets/editable_text.dart#L4939-L4961) calls `setState` only when focus is lost. On a focus gain it rebuilds only through `_handleSelectionChanged`, when `_adjustedSelectionWhenFocused()` returns a new selection, which happens only while the selection is invalid.
- `_Editable` hands `hasFocus` to `RenderEditable` from `build`, so without a rebuild the render object keeps the old value, and [`describeSemanticsConfiguration`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/5fc346839b5d0eef006ed8404392afb4dfae428d/packages/flutter/lib/src/rendering/editable.dart#L1378) reports `isFocused = hasFocus`.
- `TextField` and `CupertinoTextField` rebuild on every focus change, which hides this for them.

Workaround: rebuild the widget that owns the `EditableText` whenever its focus node changes.

