### Cause

The scrollable role stays `SemanticScrollable` when the list stops scrolling, because the role follows `hasImplicitScrolling` ([master](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/087a1b62b8996c328f12708c46ca060dba5fdf1d/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/semantics/semantics.dart#L1831)). The scroll actions go away, so `_canScroll` turns false. In `SemanticScrollable.update`:

1. `if (!_canScroll) { _cleanUp(); return; }` ([3.47.7](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/abaf9c523780a608bd46686fd5e53740a07077f8/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/semantics/scrollable.dart#L117-L120), [master](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/087a1b62b8996c328f12708c46ca060dba5fdf1d/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/semantics/scrollable.dart#L124-L127)). `_cleanUp()` ([3.47.7](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/abaf9c523780a608bd46686fd5e53740a07077f8/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/semantics/scrollable.dart#L269-L284), [master](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/087a1b62b8996c328f12708c46ca060dba5fdf1d/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/semantics/scrollable.dart#L276-L291)) removes the overflow element and the listeners. It does not touch `verticalScrollAdjustment` / `horizontalScrollAdjustment` or `scrollTop` / `scrollLeft`.
2. The adjustments were last set from `element.scrollTop` / `element.scrollLeft` in `_updateScrollableState` ([3.47.7](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/abaf9c523780a608bd46686fd5e53740a07077f8/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/semantics/scrollable.dart#L211-L222), [master](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/087a1b62b8996c328f12708c46ca060dba5fdf1d/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/semantics/scrollable.dart#L218-L229)). `recomputeChildrenAdjustment` keeps adding them to every child's translation ([3.47.7](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/abaf9c523780a608bd46686fd5e53740a07077f8/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/semantics/semantics.dart#L2511-L2512), [master](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/087a1b62b8996c328f12708c46ca060dba5fdf1d/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/semantics/semantics.dart#L2593-L2594)).
3. `_updateScrollableState` already has a branch that does the reset this case needs: `scrollLeft` and `scrollTop` to 0, both adjustments to 0 ([3.47.7](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/abaf9c523780a608bd46686fd5e53740a07077f8/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/semantics/scrollable.dart#L223-L233), [master](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/087a1b62b8996c328f12708c46ca060dba5fdf1d/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/semantics/scrollable.dart#L230-L240)). It is never reached for a node that stopped scrolling, because `update` returns before it registers the callback that calls `_updateScrollableState`.

`scrollTop` survives because the scroller remains a scroll container. `_cleanUp` calls `style.removeProperty('overflowY')` and `style.removeProperty('overflowX')` ([3.47.7](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/abaf9c523780a608bd46686fd5e53740a07077f8/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/semantics/scrollable.dart#L273-L274), [master](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/087a1b62b8996c328f12708c46ca060dba5fdf1d/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/semantics/scrollable.dart#L280-L281)). `CSSStyleDeclaration.removeProperty` takes hyphenated names, so in Chrome these calls remove nothing: after `style.overflowY = 'scroll'`, `removeProperty('overflowY')` leaves `scroll`, while `removeProperty('overflow-y')` clears it. Fixing those names alone would not fix this bug. Without overflow, `scrollTop` would read 0, and the nodes would be off by the full 300px.

### Suggested fix

In the `!_canScroll` branch of `update` (or in `_cleanUp`), reset `verticalScrollAdjustment` and `horizontalScrollAdjustment` to 0, set `scrollTop` / `scrollLeft` to 0, and re-position the children (`updateChildrenPositionAndSize()`). In effect, run the reset branch of `_updateScrollableState` without its overflow-element styling. I have not built an engine with this change.

### Related issues

#194549, the grow case described above. I found no other issue: I searched for `SemanticScrollable`, `verticalScrollAdjustment`, `flt-semantics-scroll-overflow`, `web semantics scroll offset wrong position`, `web semantics tap wrong item after list shrinks`, `web semantics scrollTop stale` and `web semantics list items shifted`.

